hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1541","Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abbad bin Abbad Al-Muhallabi, Zayd bin Ahram Al-Tai, and Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Azdi told us, they said: Abd told us Allah bin Dawud, Salamah bin Nubait narrated to us, on the authority of Nu`aym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Nubait bin Shurayt, on the authority of Salim bin Ubaid, he said: He fell ill. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then fainted, then he woke up and said: “Have you attended the prayer?” I said: Yes. He said: “Tell Bilal so that he may give the call to prayer, and tell Abu Bakr so that he may lead the people in prayer.” So they mentioned the hadith, and they said in the hadith: He called the call to prayer and established the iqama, and they ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, then he woke up and said: “The prayer was established?!” I said: Yes. He said: “Bring me a man to rely on.” They brought a girl and another man, so he relied on them, then he went out to pray, and I sat next to my father. Bakr, so Abu Bakr went to step aside, so he held him until he finished praying. Then they mentioned the hadith, and this is the hadith of Al-Qasim"
